# === Privacy guardrails ===
# Anything in these patterns will NOT be committed even if accidentally placed here.
# This file is the safety net — keep adding patterns as your private data evolves.

# === your-input/ folder — designated drop-zone for personal data ===
# Everything inside is gitignored EXCEPT the README that explains what to put here.
# Drop your CV, preferences, target-companies, etc. into this folder.
your-input/*
!your-input/.gitkeep
!your-input/README.md
# Example files are committed so newcomers can copy them; your real cv.md /
# preferences.md / companies.md / config.md stay ignored.
!your-input/*.example.md

# Personal memory / career artifacts (your local life)
# Genericized so this public file doesn't leak real local folder names.
# Add your own personal folder names here if you keep them near the repo.
career/
job-hunting/
story-box/
*-memory/

# Local secrets and config
.env
.env.*
*.private.md
*-personal.md
*-secret.md
secrets/
private/
draft/

# Scheduler / automation artifacts that contain personal info
# NOTE: the public template scheduler-prompt-template.md is intentionally NOT ignored.
SKILL.md
scheduler-prompt.md
sheet-id.txt

# Original (un-sanitized) source documents — keep these in the private parent folder only
*-narrative.md
notes-*.md

# Local OS clutter
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Editor caches
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo

# Logs and temp
*.log
*.tmp
*~

# Node / Python in case you add code later
node_modules/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/

# Generated files
build/
dist/
out/

# Sensitive samples (your specific company picks, real job IDs, etc.)
*-with-real-companies.*
*-with-real-jobs.*
